invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: rsa_mont.c chooses its arm on a define no build passes, so a host
  object compiles the 32-bit arithmetic and never calls rsa_mont64.c.
  Every answer stays right and every test of the verifiers passes, at
  the device object's speed. test/widemul-builds.sh compiles the file as
  a host object does and requires its calls into rsa_mont64.c.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME

#include "ct.h"
#include "rsa_mont64.h"
--- new
#ifdef CH_CPU_HOST

#include "ct.h"
#include "rsa_mont64.h"
